c{\\pi }{2}$ radians counterclockwise about the origin.\n\nTherefore, in order to find $Av$, we need to rotate $v$ counterclockwise by an angle of $\\frac{\\pi }{2}$ radians, as shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14068585/assets/dd0496914b35f969896c6a54907fbfa5ea6c139c878d8682b933a8757bde7524.png)"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186286123 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "b4df33ff-e04e-55ec-b273-9eceff7db53b" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Rotation Matrices"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "bf3c118a-93f1-5a86-bf30-b0f8eaf85b3e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14003089/assets/e3fe0bfa8161108c3d5edc48a6df4a52fe2c5b4dbf1c9964cf82e4f257ff357c.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186286125} {:answer/id #uuid "e20e2989-5197-5f02-89fc-96cda30ba61f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14003089/assets/cf449d44237c85963bf4fbb134da290b39aac4ebd0b128313052cbd1970db67f.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186286126} {:answer/id #uuid "87f065e9-8ca0-5637-9ddd-76dec9b86fbd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14003089/assets/979157d993a86617fabf4b2dfacc6d4c1d973885b42be081b4bcffb36058e091.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186286127} {:answer/id #uuid "e4827f5b-a4a1-556a-86e7-4a07bd2d6e9e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14003089/assets/4bf42e3bdeb61feccd68cf4eeb9e3c4a40e8b903a5739df77c993e9aa4abc993.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186286128} {:answer/id #uuid "8ef96b34-9af2-541f-9f26-8660063b1119" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/r